From 26f11322767d9e932dbbf8ee626379f1528c347c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hibreak <hibreak@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:21:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sf: e-ink render pass, the frame as the panel will show it

SurfaceFlinger now turns the composed frame into exactly what the e-ink
panel shows, so the kernel has nothing left to guess
(debug.sf.eink_render=3, the default while debug.sf.eink_enhance is on;
2 = the enhancement pass of 0009/0011/0012, unchanged, for comparison).

Why: the kernel dithers NORMAL (DU) frames with an Atkinson error
diffusion (threshold 150, 1/8 of the previous frame mixed in), so a
change anywhere moves the dither pattern elsewhere and the old screen
imprints into the greys of the new one; FAST (A2) frames are not
dithered at all, so every grey becomes a partial drive that lands on an
unstable grey (residue after scrolling); and the contrast stretch that
hid light-grey speckle also erased cards, fields, separators and photo
tones (docs/lessons-learned.md, scripts/eink-bench).

What the pass does, by the composer's refresh mode:
- NORMAL: anti-aliased edges snap to the local extremes (as before);
  thin strokes, whose surroundings out to 3 x 3.5 px are mostly on the
  other side of the local mid level, become pure black or white: grey
  text of any weight is solid, while the wide fill around white labels
  keeps its tone (no halo); low-contrast steps between light flat tones
  become a 1-px line (dotted below 10 % contrast) before light greys are
  bleached to white, so cards, fields, chips and grid lines stay visible;
  a dithered fill pixel touching a light label becomes white, so white
  text on grey or coloured buttons gets a clear 1-px margin; dark greys
  are crushed to black; then a tone curve (power 1.25 for the
  panel's dot gain, measured with a camera) and an ordered dither with a
  64x64 blue-noise map to pure black and white.
- FAST and HYPER: the same full pass by default (FAST is also the typing
  mode, so key outlines and solid text must stay, and nothing changes
  look when a scroll ends); debug.sf.eink.fast_full=0 gives a cheap
  version (tone curve and dither only), still pure black and white.
- HD, CLEAN and the grey waveforms: 16 levels sent as 16 * level + 4,
  which the kernel's 16-level dither passes unchanged.

Tunable at runtime: debug.sf.eink.{minority0_x1000 (500), minority1_x1000
(650), minspread_x1000 (250), contour (1), contour0_x1000 (30),
contourmax_x1000 (320), contourlight_x1000 (750), contoursolid_x1000
(100), gamma_x100 (125), gamma16_x100 (125), mintone_x1000 (1000: every
thin stroke solid; e.g. 350 keeps links on web pages grey), knock (1)};
the contrast setting of
HiBreakParts sets vendor.xrz.hibreak_eink_{bleach (194), crush (92)}, and
its per-app "inverted" mode vendor.xrz.hibreak_eink_invert (the frame's
lightness is inverted first, for apps that are always dark; screenshots
are not inverted).

Change-Id: I4312512632d315717b893c11929990b2be4c5d15
